course: dictionary
lesson: 13081
title: First in, first out
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: FIFO stands for first in, first out. It is a rule for queues: the first thing to join is the first thing to leave. «The first child in the lunch line is served first.» That is FIFO.
explain: You will meet FIFO in computing and maths. Picture a bus stop: nobody pushes to the front, so the person who arrived first gets on the bus first. «The printer works in FIFO order.» That means the job sent first is printed first.
explain: In Australia, FIFO can also mean fly-in fly-out. «Dad is a FIFO worker.» He flies to a far-away mine, works for some weeks, then flies home. The letters are the same, but the meaning changes, so check the context.
fact: FIFO means first in, first out.
fact: FIFO describes a queue: the first person in the line is served first.
fact: The opposite of FIFO is LIFO, last in, first out, like a stack of plates where you take the top plate first.
fact: In Australia, «FIFO» can mean fly-in fly-out: a worker flies to a far-away job, such as a mine, and flies home after some weeks.
fact: Many children in Western Australia and Queensland have a FIFO parent.
exercise: In a lunch queue, who is served first? | The tallest child | *The first child to arrive | The last child to arrive | The child who shouts loudest
exercise: What is the opposite of FIFO? | Lunch in, lunch out | Fly in, fly out | *Last in, first out | First in, first out
exercise: «Dad is a FIFO worker.» In Australia, what does FIFO mean here? | A teacher who works at one school all year | *A worker who flies to a far-away job and flies home after some weeks | A computer that stores files
test: In a stack of plates, which plate do you take first? | The plate with a crack | *The top plate | The bottom plate | The plate in the middle
test: Which rule describes a queue at a bus stop? | Fly-in fly-out | *FIFO, first in, first out | LIFO, last in, first out | Work all day, sleep all night
exam: «The computer handles printing jobs in FIFO order.» What does this tell you? | *The job that arrived first is printed first | Printing happens only at night | The newest job is printed first | The printer is broken
